---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Newsletter from '../components/Newsletter.astro';
import { SITE, url } from '../consts';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={`What ${SITE.name} is, how each project is built, and who writes it.`}>
  <article class="wrap about">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>Research for people who invest their own money</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        {SITE.name} is a weekly research series. Each week, one project takes a single firm, a
        geopolitical event, or a market situation and asks the questions a strategist would ask:
        who are the players, what do they want, what can they credibly threaten or promise, and
        where does the money end up?
      </p>

      <h2>The method</h2>
      <p>Every project runs through the same three lenses.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Game theory.</strong> Map the players, their options, and their payoffs. Most
          market "surprises" are equilibria that were visible in advance to anyone who drew the
          board.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Geopolitics.</strong> States, regulators, and alliances set the rules that
          firms play by. Ignoring them is how investors get blindsided by a tariff, a sanction, or
          an export license.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Finance.</strong> Translate the strategic picture into things that show up in
          a filing: margins, capital allocation, balance-sheet risk, and the price the market is
          charging for all of it.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Each project ends with a short box of takeaways for investors. They are not stock picks.
        They are the questions to ask and the signposts to watch.
      </p>

      <h2>Who writes it</h2>
      <!-- TODO: replace this placeholder bio with your own. -->
      <p>
        {SITE.author} writes {SITE.name}. Aidan works in banking, has passed CFA Level I, and is
        sitting Level II in 2027. This series exists because most writing for everyday investors
        is either too shallow to act on or too technical to read.
      </p>

      <h2>Cadence</h2>
      <p>
        One project a week. The <a href={url('/projects')}>archive</a> is sorted newest first and
        filterable by tag. There is an <a href={url('/rss.xml')}>RSS feed</a>, and a newsletter
        below for anyone who prefers email.
      </p>

      <h2>Disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        Everything on this site is educational content, not investment advice. The author may hold
        positions in securities discussed. Nothing here is a recommendation to buy or sell anything.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <Newsletter />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-top: 3rem;
  }
  .about h1 {
    max-width: 24ch;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
</style>
